From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cool-retro-term-wezterm <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:35:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] CRT: flat title bar with window buttons, mouse mapping,
 full screen auto-hide

- the CRT passes only cover the terminal area; the tab bar (which holds
  the integrated window buttons) and OS borders are copied unprocessed
- mouse positions over the curved screen are mapped through the same
  distortion as the shader, so selection/clicks hit what is displayed
- full screen: the tab bar is hidden (panes keep the whole screen) and
  slides in over the CRT image when the mouse touches the edge
  (crt.fullscreen_autohide_tab_bar, default on)
- windows: no top/bottom resize hit areas in full screen, so the screen
  edges deliver normal mouse events

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
